From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hero Siege Offline Toolkit <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] runner interface: rank pages, keep a scan hint on disk

Why: Hero Siege is a GameMaker YYC x64 build whose .text is at least 190 MB (the interface chain sits at RVA 0xB5557E2; the section size itself was not read), and upstream finds the RunnerInterface chain by disassembling that section page by page, first to last, on every launch, behind a "Please wait ... up to a minute" message. The modified DLL this toolkit shipped avoided that with a cache file next to the executable, but on a cache hit it planted the mid-function hook at an address read straight from that file, checking nothing but the executable's size. A stale or hand-edited file therefore patched game code at an arbitrary address, and stayed wrong on every later launch. This patch re-creates the intent as original code: a byte-level lea/mov-to-stack density ranker decides which pages the UNCHANGED upstream page scan visits first (every other page still follows, each page once), and <exe>.yytkcache is demoted to a hint whose chain RVA only selects the pages scanned first (the page it names and the page before it). The hook address is never read back from disk; acceptance and MmCreateMidfunctionHook placement always come from the upstream scan of bytes mapped in this process. Every launch that reaches the ranked scan says in one line whether the ranking found the chain ("RI pre-filter hit") or the chain was only reached in the address-order remainder ("RI pre-filter miss"), so a ranker that ranks the wrong pages cannot pass for one that works.

Evidence: evidence/fresh-build-crash.YYToolkit.log:1 (base 0x00007FF7D2F80000), :3 (cache hit at offset 0xB555351, no scan), :17 (first chain instruction 0x7ff7de4d57e2, i.e. RVA 0xB5557E2), :17-219 (100 lea/store pairs using 48 8D 0D, 48 89 4C 24 xx, 48 89 4D xx, 48 89 8D xx xx xx xx and one interrupting mov edx - the encodings the host test reproduces). The unchecked hook placement is documented/Generic-RunnerInterfaceNew.cpp:450-476. ForgePact/src/forgepact.py:268-290 (ensure_ri_cache) is a second writer of the same file: three decimal numbers keyed on the size, written by Python with CRLF, compared on token 1 only - so the legacy line stays readable and the 6 number line survives it. YYToolkit/hs-tests/ri_scan_test.cpp: 166 checks pass, also under /fsanitize=address. YYToolkit/hs-tests/ri_memory_test.cpp: 42 checks pass against real VirtualAlloc regions (reserved tail, PAGE_NOACCESS hole, guard page, PAGE_EXECUTE page, decommitted page, wrap-around; not run under /fsanitize=address); the same run read a PAGE_EXECUTE page on this x64 host without a fault, which the allow-list refuses all the same. 12 single-line mutations of the two helper headers (the ModRM mask, the gap limit at 5/6/8, each 32-bit identity limit, the ranked-visit boundary, the page before the hint, the preferred count, the region walk, PAGE_EXECUTE allowed, the guard test removed) each fail at least one check. NOT verified: no launch of the game was made with this patch; how long the scan takes with or without the pre-filter (no log has timed either, and the byte pass still pages all of .text in on a cold launch); whether the ranker ranks this game's chain page among its 64 (the "RI pre-filter hit" line of the first launch without a hint is what shows it); whether any build's chain crosses a page boundary (the page-before-the-hint rule is REASONED from upstream's 88..103 test, not reproduced); whether Internal::PpiGetModuleSectionBounds reports the virtual or the raw size (hence the bounds and VirtualQuery checks instead of trust); whether the PE CheckSum is non-zero on this game; whether Aurie's MmCreateMidfunctionHook validates its target, or can itself return AURIE_OBJECT_NOT_FOUND (Aurie's source is not in the tree, hence the WasChainAccepted out-parameter instead of reading a page miss out of the status); the Win32 configuration.

Fails-safe: Nothing read from the file can place the hook. Unreadable, empty, garbage, overlong, signed, hexadecimal or truncated lines, and a chain RVA outside .text, log one "RI scan hint miss" line and fall through to the ranked scan. A key mismatch (size, TimeDateStamp, SizeOfImage, CheckSum from the mapped headers; the file is never hashed) is only logged - the hinted pages are still tried, because the scan validates them. A hint without the chain costs two pages of disassembly, then the ranked scan runs over all remaining pages. The page before the hinted one is scanned first, in upstream's order, so a stale or hand-edited hint that names the page a chain continues on cannot get the middle of that chain accepted as its start and then written back as a matching hint (upstream itself has the same weakness when fewer than four pairs sit on the first page; that is unchanged). If the chain is accepted on a hinted page but the hook cannot be created, one "RI scan hint hook failed" line says so and the status is returned at once - the rest of .text is not disassembled for a hook that would be attempted at the same place, and the failure is never reported as a hint miss. If the PE headers cannot be queried, .text exceeds SizeOfImage, or .text is not committed memory whose protection is on an allow-list of readable protections from start to end (PAGE_EXECUTE alone is refused), hint and pre-filter are both refused with one line and the scan runs in upstream's order. Pages the ranker misses are still scanned, in address order, after the ranked ones, and the "RI pre-filter miss" line then names the page and the visit it was found at; pages linked by a run that crosses a page boundary keep their address order, as upstream would see them. If no page holds the chain, "RI scan found no chain" says how many were scanned. The file is rewritten only when the stored line differs, never when the size of the executable is unknown, and not atomically on purpose: a half-written file is merely a bad hint. The path is queried with a growing buffer (no MAX_PATH truncation) and never logged. Also guards upstream's (iterator - 1) dereference when sub rsp is the last decoded instruction, and sets m_RunnerInterfaceBase before the hook can fire (reset to 0 if the hook cannot be created). Residual: visiting pages in another order changes which site wins if more than one site in .text passes upstream's 88..103 lea test (upstream's own TODO) - the hinted pages and the ranked pages are both seen before the rest; the legacy-compatible line keeps an older, unvalidating DLL trusting token 2 until that DLL is replaced.

Log-markers: "RI scan hint hit"
Log-markers: "RI scan hint miss"
Log-markers: "RI scan hint key mismatch"
Log-markers: "RI scan hint refused"
Log-markers: "RI scan hint written"
Log-markers: "RI scan hint not written"
Log-markers: "RI scan hint unchanged"
Log-markers: "RI scan hint hook failed"
Log-markers: "RI pre-filter ranked"
Log-markers: "RI pre-filter hit"
Log-markers: "RI pre-filter miss"
Log-markers: "RI scan found no chain"

Upstream-status: not submitted. Upstream v4.0.1 has the plain first-to-last page scan and no hint file.

diff --git a/YYToolkit/hs-tests/ri_memory_test.cpp b/YYToolkit/hs-tests/ri_memory_test.cpp
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..073f146
--- /dev/null
+++ b/YYToolkit/hs-tests/ri_memory_test.cpp
@@ -0,0 +1,150 @@
+// Host test for Generic-RunnerInterfaceMemory.hpp - needs neither the game nor Aurie/Zydis, but it
+// does need Windows: the helper is run against real VirtualAlloc regions.
+//
+// From a "x64 Native Tools" prompt, in this directory:
+//     cl /nologo /std:c++latest /EHsc /W4 ri_memory_test.cpp && ri_memory_test.exe
+//
+// Prints one line per check and returns non-zero if any check failed.
+// Every predicate has at least one input it must accept and one it must refuse.
+
+#include "../source/YYTK/Module Internals/GameMaker/Generic/Generic-RunnerInterfaceMemory.hpp"
+
+#include <cstdio>
+
+using namespace YYTK::RiScan;
+
+static int g_ChecksRun = 0;
+static int g_ChecksFailed = 0;
+
+static void Check(
+	IN bool Condition,
+	IN const char* Name
+)
+{
+	g_ChecksRun++;
+	if (!Condition)
+		g_ChecksFailed++;
+
+	std::printf("%s  %s\n", Condition ? "ok  " : "FAIL", Name);
+}
+
+static size_t GetPageSize()
+{
+	SYSTEM_INFO system_info = {};
+	GetSystemInfo(&system_info);
+	return system_info.dwPageSize;
+}
+
+static uint64_t AddressOf(
+	IN const void* Pointer,
+	IN size_t Offset = 0
+)
+{
+	return static_cast<uint64_t>(reinterpret_cast<uintptr_t>(Pointer)) + Offset;
+}
+
+// Reads one byte, and says if that raised an exception. Not a check - see its caller.
+static bool CanReadByte(
+	IN const void* Pointer
+)
+{
+	__try
+	{
+		volatile uint8_t byte = *static_cast<const volatile uint8_t*>(Pointer);
+		(void)byte;
+		return true;
+	}
+	__except (EXCEPTION_EXECUTE_HANDLER)
+	{
+		return false;
+	}
+}
+
+static void TestProtections()
+{
+	Check(IsReadableProtection(PAGE_READONLY), "protect: PAGE_READONLY is readable");
+	Check(IsReadableProtection(PAGE_READWRITE), "protect: PAGE_READWRITE is readable");
+	Check(IsReadableProtection(PAGE_WRITECOPY), "protect: PAGE_WRITECOPY is readable");
+	Check(IsReadableProtection(PAGE_EXECUTE_READ), "protect: PAGE_EXECUTE_READ is readable (what .text is mapped as)");
+	Check(IsReadableProtection(PAGE_EXECUTE_READWRITE), "protect: PAGE_EXECUTE_READWRITE is readable (a page a hook was written to)");
+	Check(IsReadableProtection(PAGE_EXECUTE_WRITECOPY), "protect: PAGE_EXECUTE_WRITECOPY is readable");
+	Check(IsReadableProtection(PAGE_READONLY | PAGE_NOCACHE), "protect: a modifier does not take read access away");
+	Check(IsReadableProtection(PAGE_EXECUTE_READ | PAGE_WRITECOMBINE), "protect: ...neither does PAGE_WRITECOMBINE");
+
+	Check(!IsReadableProtection(0), "protect: 0 (no access information) is refused");
+	Check(!IsReadableProtection(PAGE_NOACCESS), "protect: PAGE_NOACCESS is refused");
+	Check(!IsReadableProtection(PAGE_EXECUTE), "protect: PAGE_EXECUTE is refused - not denied is not the same as readable");
+	Check(!IsReadableProtection(PAGE_READWRITE | PAGE_GUARD), "protect: a guard page is refused, whatever is below the guard");
+	Check(!IsReadableProtection(PAGE_EXECUTE_READ | PAGE_GUARD), "protect: ...an executable one too");
+	Check(!IsReadableProtection(PAGE_NOCACHE), "protect: a modifier alone is refused");
+	Check(!IsReadableProtection(PAGE_READONLY | PAGE_READWRITE), "protect: two protections at once are refused");
+}
+
+static void TestRanges()
+{
+	const size_t page_size = GetPageSize();
+
+	// Four pages reserved, the first three committed: [RW][RW][RW][reserved]
+	BYTE* block = static_cast<BYTE*>(VirtualAlloc(nullptr, 4 * page_size, MEM_RESERVE, PAGE_NOACCESS));
+	const bool is_committed = block && VirtualAlloc(block, 3 * page_size, MEM_COMMIT, PAGE_READWRITE);
+
+	Check(is_committed, "range: the test could set up its memory (every check below needs it)");
+	if (!is_committed)
+		return;
+
+	Check(IsRangeReadable(AddressOf(block), 3 * page_size), "range: three committed read-write pages are readable");
+	Check(IsRangeReadable(AddressOf(block), 1), "range: the first byte alone is readable");
+	Check(IsRangeReadable(AddressOf(block, (3 * page_size) - 1), 1), "range: the last committed byte alone is readable");
+	Check(IsRangeReadable(AddressOf(block, page_size / 2), 2 * page_size), "range: a range starting inside a page is readable");
+
+	Check(!IsRangeReadable(AddressOf(block), (3 * page_size) + 1), "range: one byte of reserved tail is refused");
+	Check(!IsRangeReadable(AddressOf(block), 4 * page_size), "range: a reserved page at the end is refused");
+	Check(!IsRangeReadable(AddressOf(block, 3 * page_size), 1), "range: a range that is reserved memory only is refused");
+	Check(!IsRangeReadable(AddressOf(block), 0), "range: an empty range is refused");
+	Check(!IsRangeReadable(UINT64_MAX - 0x10, 0x100), "range: a range that wraps around is refused");
+	Check(!IsRangeReadable(0, page_size), "range: the null page is refused");
+
+	DWORD old_protection = 0;
+
+	// Several readable regions in a row: [RW][RO][RW] is three regions, and the walk has to cross them
+	Check(VirtualProtect(block + page_size, page_size, PAGE_READONLY, &old_protection) != 0, "range: (setup) the middle page became read-only");
+	Check(IsRangeReadable(AddressOf(block), 3 * page_size), "range: three regions with different readable protections are readable");
+
+	// A hole in the middle: the first region is fine and the range is no longer than three pages,
+	// so only a walk that really looks at every region can refuse this
+	Check(VirtualProtect(block + page_size, page_size, PAGE_NOACCESS, &old_protection) != 0, "range: (setup) the middle page became PAGE_NOACCESS");
+	Check(!IsRangeReadable(AddressOf(block), 3 * page_size), "range: a PAGE_NOACCESS hole in the middle is refused");
+	Check(IsRangeReadable(AddressOf(block), page_size), "range: ...the page before the hole is still readable");
+	Check(IsRangeReadable(AddressOf(block, 2 * page_size), page_size), "range: ...and so is the page after it");
+	Check(!IsRangeReadable(AddressOf(block, page_size - 1), 2), "range: one byte into the hole is refused");
+
+	// VirtualQuery does not touch the page, so the guard stays armed however often it is asked
+	Check(VirtualProtect(block + page_size, page_size, PAGE_READWRITE | PAGE_GUARD, &old_protection) != 0, "range: (setup) the middle page became a guard page");
+	Check(!IsRangeReadable(AddressOf(block), 3 * page_size), "range: a guard page in the middle is refused");
+	Check(!IsRangeReadable(AddressOf(block), 3 * page_size), "range: ...and still is when asked again");
+
+	Check(VirtualProtect(block + page_size, page_size, PAGE_EXECUTE, &old_protection) != 0, "range: (setup) the middle page became PAGE_EXECUTE");
+	Check(!IsRangeReadable(AddressOf(block), 3 * page_size), "range: a PAGE_EXECUTE page in the middle is refused");
+
+	// Not a check: what this host does with a read of that PAGE_EXECUTE page, for the record.
+	// IsReadableProtection refuses the protection either way.
+	std::printf("info  reading a PAGE_EXECUTE page on this host %s\n", CanReadByte(block + page_size) ? "did not fault" : "faulted");
+
+	Check(VirtualProtect(block + page_size, page_size, PAGE_EXECUTE_READ, &old_protection) != 0, "range: (setup) the middle page became PAGE_EXECUTE_READ");
+	Check(IsRangeReadable(AddressOf(block), 3 * page_size), "range: read-write, execute-read, read-write is readable again");
+
+	// Decommitted memory in the middle
+	Check(VirtualFree(block + page_size, page_size, MEM_DECOMMIT) != 0, "range: (setup) the middle page was decommitted");
+	Check(!IsRangeReadable(AddressOf(block), 3 * page_size), "range: a decommitted page in the middle is refused");
+
+	VirtualFree(block, 0, MEM_RELEASE);
+}
+
+int main()
+{
+	TestProtections();
+	TestRanges();
+
+	std::printf("%d checks, %d failed\n", g_ChecksRun, g_ChecksFailed);
+	return g_ChecksFailed ? 1 : 0;
+}
diff --git a/YYToolkit/hs-tests/ri_scan_test.cpp b/YYToolkit/hs-tests/ri_scan_test.cpp
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f7aca54
--- /dev/null
+++ b/YYToolkit/hs-tests/ri_scan_test.cpp
@@ -0,0 +1,605 @@
+// Host test for Generic-RunnerInterfaceScan.hpp - needs neither the game nor Aurie/Zydis/Windows.
+//
+// From a "x64 Native Tools" prompt, in this directory:
+//     cl /nologo /std:c++latest /EHsc /W4 ri_scan_test.cpp && ri_scan_test.exe
+//
+// Prints one line per check and returns non-zero if any check failed.
+// Every predicate has at least one input it must accept and one it must refuse.
+
+#include "../source/YYTK/Module Internals/GameMaker/Generic/Generic-RunnerInterfaceScan.hpp"
+
+#include <cstdio>
+#include <initializer_list>
+#include <sstream>
+
+using namespace YYTK::RiScan;
+
+static int g_ChecksRun = 0;
+static int g_ChecksFailed = 0;
+
+static void Check(
+	IN bool Condition,
+	IN const char* Name
+)
+{
+	g_ChecksRun++;
+	if (!Condition)
+		g_ChecksFailed++;
+
+	std::printf("%s  %s\n", Condition ? "ok  " : "FAIL", Name);
+}
+
+using ByteBuffer = std::vector<uint8_t>;
+
+static void Append(
+	IN OUT ByteBuffer& Buffer,
+	IN std::initializer_list<int> Bytes
+)
+{
+	for (const int byte : Bytes)
+		Buffer.push_back(static_cast<uint8_t>(byte));
+}
+
+// lea rcx, [rip+disp32]
+static void AppendLea(IN OUT ByteBuffer& Buffer)
+{
+	Append(Buffer, { 0x48, 0x8D, 0x0D, 0x10, 0x32, 0x54, 0x00 });
+}
+
+// mov [rsp+60h], rcx
+static void AppendStoreRspDisp8(IN OUT ByteBuffer& Buffer)
+{
+	Append(Buffer, { 0x48, 0x89, 0x4C, 0x24, 0x60 });
+}
+
+// mov [rbp-80h], rcx
+static void AppendStoreRbpDisp8(IN OUT ByteBuffer& Buffer)
+{
+	Append(Buffer, { 0x48, 0x89, 0x4D, 0x80 });
+}
+
+// mov [rbp+248h], rcx
+static void AppendStoreRbpDisp32(IN OUT ByteBuffer& Buffer)
+{
+	Append(Buffer, { 0x48, 0x89, 0x8D, 0x48, 0x02, 0x00, 0x00 });
+}
+
+// mov [rsp], rcx - no displacement, never part of the chain
+static void AppendStoreRspNoDisp(IN OUT ByteBuffer& Buffer)
+{
+	Append(Buffer, { 0x48, 0x89, 0x0C, 0x24 });
+}
+
+// mov edx, 320h - the instruction that interrupts the real chain
+static void AppendMovEdx(IN OUT ByteBuffer& Buffer)
+{
+	Append(Buffer, { 0xBA, 0x20, 0x03, 0x00, 0x00 });
+}
+
+// A chain shaped like the one this game builds: rsp-relative stores first, then rbp-relative ones
+// with a short and a long displacement, and one "mov edx" between a lea and its store.
+static ByteBuffer MakeChain(IN size_t PairCount)
+{
+	ByteBuffer chain;
+
+	for (size_t pair = 0; pair < PairCount; pair++)
+	{
+		AppendLea(chain);
+
+		if (pair == 7)
+			AppendMovEdx(chain);
+
+		if (pair < 4)
+			AppendStoreRspDisp8(chain);
+		else if (pair < 20)
+			AppendStoreRbpDisp8(chain);
+		else
+			AppendStoreRbpDisp32(chain);
+	}
+
+	return chain;
+}
+
+// PageCount pages of int3 padding, which holds neither a lea nor a store.
+static ByteBuffer MakeText(
+	IN size_t PageCount,
+	IN size_t PageSize
+)
+{
+	return ByteBuffer(PageCount * PageSize, static_cast<uint8_t>(0xCC));
+}
+
+static void Place(
+	IN OUT ByteBuffer& Text,
+	IN size_t Offset,
+	IN const ByteBuffer& Bytes
+)
+{
+	for (size_t index = 0; index < Bytes.size() && (Offset + index) < Text.size(); index++)
+		Text[Offset + index] = Bytes[index];
+}
+
+static bool IsSameOrder(
+	IN const std::vector<size_t>& Actual,
+	IN std::initializer_list<size_t> Expected
+)
+{
+	return Actual == std::vector<size_t>(Expected);
+}
+
+static bool Parse(
+	IN const char* Text,
+	OUT HintLine& Line
+)
+{
+	std::istringstream stream(Text);
+	return ParseHintLine(stream, Line);
+}
+
+static void TestInstructionMatchers()
+{
+	const ByteBuffer lea_rcx = { 0x48, 0x8D, 0x0D, 0x01, 0x02, 0x03, 0x04 };
+	const ByteBuffer lea_r8 = { 0x4C, 0x8D, 0x05, 0x01, 0x02, 0x03, 0x04 };
+	const ByteBuffer lea_rsp_relative = { 0x48, 0x8D, 0x4C, 0x24, 0x60, 0xCC, 0xCC };
+	const ByteBuffer lea_32bit = { 0x8D, 0x0D, 0x01, 0x02, 0x03, 0x04, 0xCC };
+	const ByteBuffer mov_load = { 0x48, 0x8B, 0x0D, 0x01, 0x02, 0x03, 0x04 };
+
+	Check(IsRipRelativeLea(lea_rcx.data(), lea_rcx.size(), 0), "lea: accepts lea rcx, [rip+disp32]");
+	Check(IsRipRelativeLea(lea_r8.data(), lea_r8.size(), 0), "lea: accepts lea r8, [rip+disp32]");
+	Check(!IsRipRelativeLea(lea_rsp_relative.data(), lea_rsp_relative.size(), 0), "lea: refuses lea rcx, [rsp+60h]");
+	Check(!IsRipRelativeLea(lea_32bit.data(), lea_32bit.size(), 0), "lea: refuses a lea without REX.W");
+	Check(!IsRipRelativeLea(mov_load.data(), mov_load.size(), 0), "lea: refuses mov rcx, [rip+disp32]");
+	Check(!IsRipRelativeLea(lea_rcx.data(), lea_rcx.size() - 1, 0), "lea: refuses a lea cut off by the end of the buffer");
+	Check(!IsRipRelativeLea(lea_rcx.data(), lea_rcx.size(), lea_rcx.size()), "lea: refuses an offset at the end of the buffer");
+	Check(!IsRipRelativeLea(lea_rcx.data(), lea_rcx.size(), SIZE_MAX), "lea: refuses an offset far past the buffer");
+
+	// mod=00 with any rm but 101 is NOT rip-relative, and such a lea is shorter than 7 bytes -
+	// taking it for one would swallow the bytes that follow it
+	const ByteBuffer lea_register_indirect = { 0x48, 0x8D, 0x01, 0x48, 0x8D, 0x0D, 0x01 };
+	const ByteBuffer lea_sib_absolute = { 0x48, 0x8D, 0x04, 0x25, 0x01, 0x02, 0x03, 0x04 };
+	const ByteBuffer lea_rbp_disp32 = { 0x48, 0x8D, 0x8D, 0x01, 0x02, 0x03, 0x04 };
+	const ByteBuffer lea_register_form = { 0x48, 0x8D, 0xC5, 0x01, 0x02, 0x03, 0x04 };
+	Check(!IsRipRelativeLea(lea_register_indirect.data(), lea_register_indirect.size(), 0), "lea: refuses lea rax, [rcx] (mod=00, rm=001)");
+	Check(!IsRipRelativeLea(lea_sib_absolute.data(), lea_sib_absolute.size(), 0), "lea: refuses lea rax, [disp32] (mod=00, rm=100 with a SIB byte)");
+	Check(!IsRipRelativeLea(lea_rbp_disp32.data(), lea_rbp_disp32.size(), 0), "lea: refuses lea rcx, [rbp+disp32] (mod=10, rm=101)");
+	Check(!IsRipRelativeLea(lea_register_form.data(), lea_register_form.size(), 0), "lea: refuses mod=11 with rm=101");
+
+	const ByteBuffer store_rsp8 = { 0x48, 0x89, 0x4C, 0x24, 0x60 };
+	const ByteBuffer store_rbp8 = { 0x48, 0x89, 0x4D, 0x80 };
+	const ByteBuffer store_rbp32 = { 0x48, 0x89, 0x8D, 0x48, 0x02, 0x00, 0x00 };
+	const ByteBuffer store_rsp32 = { 0x48, 0x89, 0x8C, 0x24, 0x00, 0x01, 0x00, 0x00 };
+	const ByteBuffer store_r8 = { 0x4C, 0x89, 0x45, 0x90 };
+	const ByteBuffer store_rsp_no_disp = { 0x48, 0x89, 0x0C, 0x24, 0xCC, 0xCC, 0xCC, 0xCC };
+	const ByteBuffer store_register = { 0x48, 0x89, 0xC8, 0xCC, 0xCC, 0xCC, 0xCC, 0xCC };
+	const ByteBuffer store_rip_relative = { 0x48, 0x89, 0x0D, 0x01, 0x02, 0x03, 0x04, 0xCC };
+	const ByteBuffer store_rbx = { 0x48, 0x89, 0x4B, 0x10, 0xCC, 0xCC, 0xCC, 0xCC };
+	const ByteBuffer store_indexed = { 0x48, 0x89, 0x4C, 0x8C, 0x60, 0xCC, 0xCC, 0xCC };
+	const ByteBuffer load_rbp8 = { 0x48, 0x8B, 0x4D, 0x80, 0xCC, 0xCC, 0xCC, 0xCC };
+	const ByteBuffer store_r13 = { 0x49, 0x89, 0x4D, 0x80, 0xCC, 0xCC, 0xCC, 0xCC };
+
+	Check(GetStackStoreLength(store_rsp8.data(), store_rsp8.size(), 0) == 5, "store: mov [rsp+disp8], rcx is 5 bytes");
+	Check(GetStackStoreLength(store_rbp8.data(), store_rbp8.size(), 0) == 4, "store: mov [rbp+disp8], rcx is 4 bytes");
+	Check(GetStackStoreLength(store_rbp32.data(), store_rbp32.size(), 0) == 7, "store: mov [rbp+disp32], rcx is 7 bytes");
+	Check(GetStackStoreLength(store_rsp32.data(), store_rsp32.size(), 0) == 8, "store: mov [rsp+disp32], rcx is 8 bytes");
+	Check(GetStackStoreLength(store_r8.data(), store_r8.size(), 0) == 4, "store: mov [rbp+disp8], r8 is 4 bytes");
+	Check(GetStackStoreLength(store_rsp_no_disp.data(), store_rsp_no_disp.size(), 0) == 0, "store: refuses mov [rsp], rcx");
+	Check(GetStackStoreLength(store_register.data(), store_register.size(), 0) == 0, "store: refuses mov rax, rcx");
+	Check(GetStackStoreLength(store_rip_relative.data(), store_rip_relative.size(), 0) == 0, "store: refuses mov [rip+disp32], rcx");
+	Check(GetStackStoreLength(store_rbx.data(), store_rbx.size(), 0) == 0, "store: refuses mov [rbx+10h], rcx");
+	Check(GetStackStoreLength(store_indexed.data(), store_indexed.size(), 0) == 0, "store: refuses mov [rsp+rcx*4+60h], rcx");
+	Check(GetStackStoreLength(load_rbp8.data(), load_rbp8.size(), 0) == 0, "store: refuses mov rcx, [rbp-80h]");
+	Check(GetStackStoreLength(store_r13.data(), store_r13.size(), 0) == 0, "store: refuses mov [r13-80h], rcx");
+	Check(GetStackStoreLength(store_rbp32.data(), 5, 0) == 0, "store: refuses a disp32 store cut off by the end of the buffer");
+	Check(GetStackStoreLength(store_rsp8.data(), 3, 0) == 0, "store: refuses a buffer too short to hold any store");
+	Check(GetStackStoreLength(store_rsp8.data(), store_rsp8.size(), store_rsp8.size()) == 0, "store: refuses an offset at the end of the buffer");
+}
+
+static void TestPairRuns()
+{
+	const ByteBuffer chain = MakeChain(100);
+	size_t run_end = 0;
+
+	Check(MeasurePairRun(chain.data(), chain.size(), 0, run_end) == 100, "run: the 100 pair chain counts as 100 pairs");
+	Check(run_end == chain.size(), "run: the run ends where the chain ends");
+
+	// The chain holds a mov edx between a lea and its store (pair 7) - without the gap it would stop there
+	Check(MeasurePairRun(chain.data(), chain.size(), 1, run_end) == 0, "run: refuses to start on something that is not a lea");
+
+	ByteBuffer gap_before_lea;
+	AppendLea(gap_before_lea);
+	AppendStoreRbpDisp8(gap_before_lea);
+	AppendMovEdx(gap_before_lea);
+	AppendLea(gap_before_lea);
+	AppendStoreRbpDisp8(gap_before_lea);
+	Check(MeasurePairRun(gap_before_lea.data(), gap_before_lea.size(), 0, run_end) == 2, "run: a 5 byte instruction before a lea does not end the run");
+
+	ByteBuffer wide_gap;
+	AppendLea(wide_gap);
+	AppendStoreRbpDisp8(wide_gap);
+	Append(wide_gap, { 0x90, 0x90, 0x90, 0x90, 0x90, 0x90, 0x90, 0x90 });
+	AppendLea(wide_gap);
+	AppendStoreRbpDisp8(wide_gap);
+	Check(MeasurePairRun(wide_gap.data(), wide_gap.size(), 0, run_end) == 1, "run: 8 bytes of something else end the run");
+	Check(run_end == 11, "run: the run that was ended stops after its last store");
+
+	// The gap limit itself, from both sides and for both places a gap can be
+	const auto make_gapped_pairs = [](size_t GapBeforeLea, size_t GapBeforeStore) -> ByteBuffer
+		{
+			ByteBuffer pairs;
+			AppendLea(pairs);
+			AppendStoreRbpDisp8(pairs);
+			pairs.insert(pairs.end(), GapBeforeLea, static_cast<uint8_t>(0x90));
+			AppendLea(pairs);
+			pairs.insert(pairs.end(), GapBeforeStore, static_cast<uint8_t>(0x90));
+			AppendStoreRbpDisp8(pairs);
+			return pairs;
+		};
+
+	const ByteBuffer lea_gap_6 = make_gapped_pairs(6, 0);
+	const ByteBuffer lea_gap_7 = make_gapped_pairs(7, 0);
+	const ByteBuffer lea_gap_8 = make_gapped_pairs(8, 0);
+	const ByteBuffer store_gap_6 = make_gapped_pairs(0, 6);
+	const ByteBuffer store_gap_7 = make_gapped_pairs(0, 7);
+	const ByteBuffer store_gap_8 = make_gapped_pairs(0, 8);
+	const ByteBuffer both_gaps_7 = make_gapped_pairs(7, 7);
+
+	Check(MeasurePairRun(lea_gap_6.data(), lea_gap_6.size(), 0, run_end) == 2, "run: 6 bytes before a lea do not end the run");
+	Check(MeasurePairRun(lea_gap_7.data(), lea_gap_7.size(), 0, run_end) == 2, "run: exactly 7 bytes before a lea do not end the run");
+	Check(run_end == lea_gap_7.size(), "run: ...and the run ends after the second store");
+	Check(MeasurePairRun(lea_gap_8.data(), lea_gap_8.size(), 0, run_end) == 1, "run: 8 bytes before a lea end the run");
+	Check(MeasurePairRun(store_gap_6.data(), store_gap_6.size(), 0, run_end) == 2, "run: 6 bytes before a store do not end the run");
+	Check(MeasurePairRun(store_gap_7.data(), store_gap_7.size(), 0, run_end) == 2, "run: exactly 7 bytes before a store do not end the run");
+	Check(run_end == store_gap_7.size(), "run: ...and the run ends after the second store");
+	Check(MeasurePairRun(store_gap_8.data(), store_gap_8.size(), 0, run_end) == 1, "run: 8 bytes before a store end the run");
+	Check(MeasurePairRun(both_gaps_7.data(), both_gaps_7.size(), 0, run_end) == 2, "run: 7 bytes before the lea and 7 before its store do not end the run");
+
+	ByteBuffer lonely_lea;
+	AppendLea(lonely_lea);
+	Append(lonely_lea, { 0xCC, 0xCC, 0xCC, 0xCC, 0xCC, 0xCC, 0xCC, 0xCC, 0xCC, 0xCC, 0xCC, 0xCC, 0xCC, 0xCC, 0xCC, 0xCC });
+	Check(MeasurePairRun(lonely_lea.data(), lonely_lea.size(), 0, run_end) == 0, "run: a lea without a store is no pair");
+
+	// No read past the end: every truncation of the chain has to give a sane, never growing count.
+	// (Build with /fsanitize=address to have the reads themselves checked.)
+	bool is_truncation_sane = true;
+	uint32_t previous_count = 100;
+	for (size_t cut = 0; cut <= 64; cut++)
+	{
+		const ByteBuffer truncated(chain.begin(), chain.end() - static_cast<std::ptrdiff_t>(cut));
+		const uint32_t count = MeasurePairRun(truncated.data(), truncated.size(), 0, run_end);
+
+		if (count > previous_count || run_end > truncated.size())
+			is_truncation_sane = false;
+
+		previous_count = count;
+	}
+	Check(is_truncation_sane, "run: a chain cut off anywhere in its last 64 bytes never counts past the buffer");
+	Check(previous_count < 100, "run: a chain cut off by 64 bytes counts fewer pairs (the check above can fail)");
+}
+
+static void TestPageRanking()
+{
+	constexpr size_t page_size = 0x1000;
+
+	// Baseline: the chain where this game has it - 0x7E2 into a page, entirely inside it
+	{
+		ByteBuffer text = MakeText(8, page_size);
+		Place(text, (5 * page_size) + 0x7E2, MakeChain(100));
+		Check(IsSameOrder(RankPages(text.data(), text.size(), 8, page_size), { 5 }), "rank: the page with the 100 pair chain is the only ranked page");
+	}
+
+	// Dense before sparse, no matter the address
+	{
+		ByteBuffer text = MakeText(8, page_size);
+		Place(text, (2 * page_size) + 0x100, MakeChain(10));
+		Place(text, (5 * page_size) + 0x7E2, MakeChain(100));
+		Place(text, (7 * page_size) + 0x020, MakeChain(40));
+		Check(IsSameOrder(RankPages(text.data(), text.size(), 8, page_size), { 5, 7, 2 }), "rank: longest run first (100, 40, 10 pairs)");
+		Check(IsSameOrder(RankPages(text.data(), text.size(), 8, page_size, 2), { 5, 7 }), "rank: the page limit keeps the longest runs");
+	}
+
+	// Equal runs keep address order
+	{
+		ByteBuffer text = MakeText(8, page_size);
+		Place(text, (6 * page_size) + 0x300, MakeChain(30));
+		Place(text, (1 * page_size) + 0x300, MakeChain(30));
+		Check(IsSameOrder(RankPages(text.data(), text.size(), 8, page_size), { 1, 6 }), "rank: equal runs stay in address order");
+	}
+
+	// Negative controls: nothing in these may be ranked
+	{
+		ByteBuffer text = MakeText(8, page_size);
+		Place(text, (3 * page_size) + 0x10, MakeChain(3));
+		Check(RankPages(text.data(), text.size(), 8, page_size).empty(), "rank: a 3 pair run is not ranked");
+	}
+	{
+		ByteBuffer text = MakeText(8, page_size);
+		ByteBuffer no_disp_chain;
+		for (int pair = 0; pair < 100; pair++)
+		{
+			AppendLea(no_disp_chain);
+			AppendStoreRspNoDisp(no_disp_chain);
+		}
+		Place(text, (3 * page_size) + 0x10, no_disp_chain);
+		Check(RankPages(text.data(), text.size(), 8, page_size).empty(), "rank: 100 lea / mov [rsp], rcx pairs are not ranked");
+	}
+	{
+		// A fixed linear congruential sequence, so that the run is the same on every host
+		ByteBuffer text(8 * page_size);
+		uint32_t state = 0x2545F491;
+		for (uint8_t& byte : text)
+		{
+			state = (state * 1664525u) + 1013904223u;
+			byte = static_cast<uint8_t>(state >> 24);
+		}
+		Check(RankPages(text.data(), text.size(), 8, page_size).empty(), "rank: pseudo-random bytes are not ranked");
+	}
+	{
+		const ByteBuffer text = MakeText(8, page_size);
+		Check(RankPages(text.data(), text.size(), 8, page_size).empty(), "rank: padding is not ranked");
+		Check(RankPages(nullptr, text.size(), 8, page_size).empty(), "rank: no buffer, no pages");
+		Check(RankPages(text.data(), text.size(), 8, 0).empty(), "rank: a page size of 0 is refused");
+		Check(RankPages(text.data(), text.size(), 0, page_size).empty(), "rank: a page count of 0 is refused");
+	}
+
+	// A chain across a page boundary: both pages, the one it starts on first
+	{
+		ByteBuffer text = MakeText(8, page_size);
+		Place(text, (3 * page_size) + 0xF00, MakeChain(100));
+		Check(IsSameOrder(RankPages(text.data(), text.size(), 8, page_size), { 3, 4 }), "rank: a chain across a boundary ranks both pages, first page first");
+	}
+
+	// The link rule: a longer run on the page a chain continues on must not pull that page in front
+	{
+		ByteBuffer text = MakeText(8, page_size);
+		Place(text, (3 * page_size) + 0xF80, MakeChain(30));
+		Place(text, (4 * page_size) + 0x800, MakeChain(50));
+		Check(IsSameOrder(RankPages(text.data(), text.size(), 8, page_size), { 3, 4 }), "rank: the page a run starts on comes before the page it continues on");
+	}
+	{
+		// Same two runs, but the shorter one ends before the boundary: now the longer run does win
+		ByteBuffer text = MakeText(8, page_size);
+		Place(text, (3 * page_size) + 0x100, MakeChain(30));
+		Place(text, (4 * page_size) + 0x800, MakeChain(50));
+		Check(IsSameOrder(RankPages(text.data(), text.size(), 8, page_size), { 4, 3 }), "rank: without a run across the boundary the longer run comes first");
+	}
+
+	// The page size really is a parameter
+	{
+		ByteBuffer text = MakeText(16, 256);
+		Place(text, (5 * 256) + 0x10, MakeChain(10));
+		const std::vector<size_t> ranked = RankPages(text.data(), text.size(), 16, 256);
+		Check(!ranked.empty() && ranked.front() == 5, "rank: 256 byte pages are ranked by 256 byte pages");
+	}
+
+	// A chain running into the end of the buffer, and a page count smaller than the buffer
+	{
+		ByteBuffer text = MakeText(2, page_size);
+		Place(text, (2 * page_size) - 0x40, MakeChain(100));
+		Check(IsSameOrder(RankPages(text.data(), text.size(), 2, page_size), { 1 }), "rank: a chain cut off by the end of the buffer ranks its page");
+		Check(RankPages(text.data(), text.size(), 1, page_size).empty(), "rank: a page past the page count is never returned");
+	}
+}
+
+static std::vector<size_t> Order(
+	IN std::initializer_list<size_t> PreferredPages,
+	IN size_t PageCount,
+	IN std::initializer_list<size_t> SkippedPages,
+	OUT size_t& PreferredVisitCount
+)
+{
+	return BuildPageVisitOrder(
+		std::vector<size_t>(PreferredPages),
+		PageCount,
+		std::vector<size_t>(SkippedPages),
+		PreferredVisitCount
+	);
+}
+
+static void TestVisitOrder()
+{
+	size_t preferred = 99;
+
+	Check(IsSameOrder(Order({ 5, 2 }, 8, {}, preferred), { 5, 2, 0, 1, 3, 4, 6, 7 }), "order: preferred pages first, then the rest in address order");
+	Check(preferred == 2, "order: ...and both preferred pages are counted as leading the order");
+	Check(IsSameOrder(Order({}, 4, {}, preferred), { 0, 1, 2, 3 }), "order: nothing preferred gives upstream's order");
+	Check(preferred == 0, "order: ...and no page is counted as preferred");
+	Check(IsSameOrder(Order({ 5, 2 }, 8, { 5 }, preferred), { 2, 0, 1, 3, 4, 6, 7 }), "order: a skipped page is left out, even if preferred");
+	Check(preferred == 1, "order: ...and a preferred page that was skipped is not counted");
+	Check(IsSameOrder(Order({ 5, 2 }, 8, { 6 }, preferred), { 5, 2, 0, 1, 3, 4, 7 }), "order: a skipped page is left out of the rest");
+	Check(IsSameOrder(Order({ 5, 2 }, 8, { 4, 5 }, preferred), { 2, 0, 1, 3, 6, 7 }), "order: both pages scanned for a hint are left out");
+	Check(preferred == 1, "order: ...and only the preferred page that is left is counted");
+	Check(IsSameOrder(Order({ 9, 2, 2, 100 }, 4, {}, preferred), { 2, 0, 1, 3 }), "order: repeated and out of range preferred pages are dropped");
+	Check(preferred == 1, "order: ...and dropped preferred pages are not counted");
+	Check(IsSameOrder(Order({ 1 }, 4, { 100 }, preferred), { 1, 0, 2, 3 }), "order: a skipped page out of range changes nothing");
+	Check(IsSameOrder(Order({ 1 }, 4, { 0, 1, 2, 3 }, preferred), {}), "order: every page skipped leaves nothing to visit");
+	Check(preferred == 0, "order: ...and nothing is counted");
+	Check(Order({ 1 }, 0, {}, preferred).empty() && preferred == 0, "order: no pages, no order");
+
+	// "Did the ranking bring the page to the front?" - decides between the pre-filter hit and miss lines
+	Check(IsVisitIndexRanked(0, 2), "ranked: the first visit of two ranked pages is a ranked one");
+	Check(IsVisitIndexRanked(1, 2), "ranked: the last ranked visit is a ranked one");
+	Check(!IsVisitIndexRanked(2, 2), "ranked: the first visit after the ranked pages is not");
+	Check(!IsVisitIndexRanked(0, 0), "ranked: nothing is ranked if no ranked page leads the order");
+	Check(!IsVisitIndexRanked(SIZE_MAX, 64), "ranked: a visit far down the address-order remainder is not");
+
+	// The two ends of the same question, through the order itself: page 5 is ranked, page 6 is not
+	{
+		const std::vector<size_t> order = Order({ 5, 2 }, 8, {}, preferred);
+		const size_t visit_of_page_5 = static_cast<size_t>(std::find(order.begin(), order.end(), size_t(5)) - order.begin());
+		const size_t visit_of_page_6 = static_cast<size_t>(std::find(order.begin(), order.end(), size_t(6)) - order.begin());
+		Check(IsVisitIndexRanked(visit_of_page_5, preferred), "ranked: a chain on a ranked page is reported as a hit");
+		Check(!IsVisitIndexRanked(visit_of_page_6, preferred), "ranked: a chain on an unranked page is reported as a miss");
+	}
+
+	// The pages scanned for a hint
+	Check(IsSameOrder(BuildHintVisitOrder(5, 8), { 4, 5 }), "hint order: the page before the hinted one is scanned first");
+	Check(IsSameOrder(BuildHintVisitOrder(0, 8), { 0 }), "hint order: page 0 has no page before it");
+	Check(IsSameOrder(BuildHintVisitOrder(7, 8), { 6, 7 }), "hint order: the last page is a valid hint");
+	Check(BuildHintVisitOrder(8, 8).empty(), "hint order: a page past the section is refused");
+	Check(BuildHintVisitOrder(SIZE_MAX, 8).empty(), "hint order: a huge page is refused");
+	Check(BuildHintVisitOrder(0, 0).empty(), "hint order: no pages, no order");
+
+	// A stale hint that names the page a chain CONTINUES on must see the page it starts on first -
+	// the same order the ranking gives those two pages, and the one upstream scans them in.
+	{
+		constexpr size_t page_size = 0x1000;
+		ByteBuffer text = MakeText(8, page_size);
+		Place(text, (3 * page_size) + 0xF80, MakeChain(100));
+
+		size_t continuation_page = 0;
+		const bool is_on_page_4 = GetPageOfRva(0x1000 + (4 * page_size) + 0x10, 0x1000, 8 * page_size, page_size, continuation_page) && continuation_page == 4;
+		Check(is_on_page_4, "hint order: an rva past the boundary names the page the chain continues on");
+		Check(BuildHintVisitOrder(continuation_page, 8) == RankPages(text.data(), text.size(), 8, page_size), "hint order: ...and the hint scans the same pages, in the same order, as the ranking (3, then 4)");
+		Check(BuildHintVisitOrder(continuation_page, 8).front() == 3, "hint order: ...starting with the page the chain starts on");
+	}
+}
